SECRETS

- (secrets) gives alist of (key . description) ; values hidden.
- (secret "REPL_TOKEN") gives value as tainted string. Works in all string
  functions; taint flows into every result computed from it. Prints redacted:
  hash-and-angle-brackets printout naming only key. Revealed only when
  serialized into outgoing MCP call argument or header.
  Only REPL_-prefixed keys visible.
  Example: (load-mcp :name "acme" :url "…" :headers (list (cons "Authorization" (secret "REPL_ACME_TOKEN")))) .

GOTCHAS

- Printout cannot be read back. Typing one into a form always errors. Call
  (secret "KEY") again, or use name you bound it to.
